WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:04.270
For instance,
even if those arms of yours

00:04.270 --> 00:07.100
Become entwined in chains

00:07.100 --> 00:10.540
For instance,
even if this space we live in

00:10.540 --> 00:14.910
Someday will burn completely down

00:14.910 --> 00:21.040
Keep believing in hope, if nothing else

00:22.320 --> 00:26.580
In the shadows of glimmering stars

00:28.390 --> 00:32.660
There is a world governed by darkness

00:34.460 --> 00:38.960
Just one life that is out there

00:40.470 --> 00:45.740
If you keep it entrapped there,
lonely boy

00:46.540 --> 00:52.310
The reason that we met each other here

00:52.310 --> 00:58.650
Must surely exist

00:58.650 --> 01:01.920
For instance,
even if sorrow takes you

01:01.920 --> 01:04.860
And you're about to collapse under it

01:04.860 --> 01:08.200
For instance,
if my chest can become

01:08.200 --> 01:12.570
A power to hold you and keep you there

01:12.570 --> 01:16.970
I'm sure that even
tomorrow we can survive

01:27.320 --> 01:31.450
This is a marine planet with
99% of the surface covered by water.

01:31.450 --> 01:34.490
Atmosphere consists mainly
of nitrogen and oxygen.

01:34.490 --> 01:37.080
The conditions for
human life are met here...

01:39.530 --> 01:41.260
I see an island.

01:41.260 --> 01:43.600
It appears that the
inhabitants are humanoid.

01:43.600 --> 01:46.430
The remains of a colonization
ship is on the ocean floor.

01:48.170 --> 01:50.660
I guess we'll go say
hello to our comrades.

01:55.380 --> 01:57.000
Such a beautiful planet...

01:59.780 --> 02:02.320
- What is it?
- Enemy on the planet's other side!

02:02.320 --> 02:03.650
L-Let's run for it!

02:03.650 --> 02:06.620
- How many?
- A dozen or so cube types, uh...

02:06.620 --> 02:08.590
And I see some strange contraption.

02:11.930 --> 02:13.590
What is that?

02:25.510 --> 02:26.630
All right!

02:29.880 --> 02:31.150
So it's finally here.

02:31.150 --> 02:32.110
Listen.

02:32.110 --> 02:35.410
This time, you're finally
going to combine with me.

02:36.580 --> 02:37.590
Well?

02:37.590 --> 02:38.720
Wasn't it great?

02:38.720 --> 02:39.710
Perfect!

02:41.120 --> 02:42.250
How stupid...

02:44.460 --> 02:45.490
Hold it!

02:45.490 --> 02:47.560
I'm not done talking to you yet!

02:47.560 --> 02:50.800
Argh, this calls for
the second stage, Barnette!

02:50.800 --> 02:51.860
I know.

03:04.980 --> 03:07.350
Well? Want to combine now?

03:07.350 --> 03:09.440
- Damn you!
- Mr. Alien, look out!

03:11.890 --> 03:14.920
If you're gonna combine,
do it with me!

03:14.920 --> 03:17.930
Sheesh, each and every one of you!

03:17.930 --> 03:19.290
You're all annoying!

03:23.460 --> 03:26.870
Damn it, they learned how to dodge...

03:26.870 --> 03:30.510
The enemy's maneuvers
are far better than before.

03:30.510 --> 03:32.910
They're reading our cards now.

03:32.910 --> 03:34.740
What despicable enemies.

03:34.740 --> 03:37.150
- Everyone, listen up!
- Jura?

03:37.150 --> 03:40.620
Today's the day I finally show
off my elegant transformation!

03:40.620 --> 03:41.880
There she goes again.

03:41.880 --> 03:43.550
Don't decide that on your own!

03:43.550 --> 03:45.610
Who'd want to combine with you?

03:48.590 --> 03:49.960
Do your job seriously!

03:49.960 --> 03:51.290
Quit fooling around!

04:00.770 --> 04:01.630
Don't look away!

04:07.110 --> 04:08.100
Mr. Alien!

04:10.450 --> 04:11.430
No!

04:13.750 --> 04:16.820
Geez, I can't get close to Mr. Alien!

04:16.820 --> 04:17.940
Dita, eyes front!

04:21.660 --> 04:22.760
Jura?

04:22.760 --> 04:24.620
They're entering the atmosphere!

04:29.030 --> 04:30.870
Hot!

04:30.870 --> 04:32.490
I don't wanna be roasted!

04:33.670 --> 04:36.070
Barnette, is the camera rolling?

04:36.070 --> 04:37.500
Is this really the time?

04:39.810 --> 04:40.880
Just watch!

04:40.880 --> 04:42.570
The third stage is starting!

04:45.710 --> 04:47.200
- Jura!
- Mr. Alien!

04:52.020 --> 04:54.920
They've landed on the water near the city!

04:54.920 --> 04:56.420
Jura! Hibiki!

04:56.420 --> 04:57.520
Are you all right? Respond!

05:01.260 --> 05:03.130
Jura, it can't be...

05:03.130 --> 05:05.130
What? What happened?

05:05.130 --> 05:06.430
Jura! Hibiki!

05:30.560 --> 05:32.930
Another new one came out.

05:32.930 --> 05:34.660
However, that's...

05:36.430 --> 05:37.500
A crab.

05:37.500 --> 05:39.670
N-No!

05:39.670 --> 05:42.570
This just can't be mine!

05:44.570 --> 05:47.810
Damn it, how do I move this thing?

05:47.810 --> 05:49.310
Shut up!

05:49.310 --> 05:50.580
This isn't the time!

05:50.580 --> 05:51.980
We have to fight back!

05:51.980 --> 05:53.040
No!

05:58.150 --> 06:00.360
Crap, where are the weapons?

06:00.360 --> 06:01.340
The weapons?

06:04.460 --> 06:05.930
This doesn't look good.

06:05.930 --> 06:07.600
They're headed towards the ocean city.

06:07.600 --> 06:09.560
What about Meia and Dita?

06:09.560 --> 06:11.660
They're still engaging
the enemy in orbit!

06:16.040 --> 06:18.510
She sure is doing whatever she wants.

06:18.510 --> 06:20.580
I've had enough! Let me off!

06:20.580 --> 06:21.640
Shut up!

06:21.640 --> 06:22.970
Help out a bit here!

06:23.980 --> 06:24.970
This one?

06:29.450 --> 06:30.780
This is okay, too.

06:34.720 --> 06:36.020
What is this?

06:37.020 --> 06:38.290
It looks horrible!

06:38.290 --> 06:39.260
Shut up!

06:39.260 --> 06:41.730
If you have the time to
complain, then look for weapons!

06:41.730 --> 06:43.800
No! Let me off this thing!

06:43.800 --> 06:45.530
Be quiet for a bit!

06:45.530 --> 06:46.860
What about this one?

06:58.150 --> 06:59.170
All right!

07:05.650 --> 07:08.060
The cube-type enemies
have been destroyed.

07:08.060 --> 07:11.230
But our attacks are unable to
damage that strange machine.

07:11.230 --> 07:12.890
You can come back for now.

07:12.890 --> 07:14.030
Good job.

07:14.030 --> 07:14.960
Roger.

07:16.660 --> 07:18.200
Could that be

07:18.200 --> 07:19.900
a machine for the "harvest"?

07:19.900 --> 07:21.770
I don't know.

07:21.770 --> 07:24.100
Why don't we ask
the people down there?

07:31.180 --> 07:33.210
I saw your elegance!

07:33.210 --> 07:36.250
I have it perfectly stored on film.

07:36.250 --> 07:37.220
Jura!

07:37.220 --> 07:38.820
Jura, can you hear me?

07:38.820 --> 07:39.790
Answer me!

07:41.790 --> 07:43.490
We can communicate!

07:43.490 --> 07:45.230
Put them on the main monitor.

07:45.230 --> 07:46.220
Sure!

07:48.030 --> 07:49.330
Hello.

07:49.330 --> 07:51.300
My name is Fanieta.

07:51.300 --> 07:55.290
Welcome to Anpathos, the most
beautiful planet in the universe.

07:56.300 --> 07:57.710
Anpathos?

07:57.710 --> 07:59.510
Is that your planet's name?

07:59.510 --> 08:00.810
That is correct.

08:00.810 --> 08:03.310
This is what we have been calling it.

08:03.310 --> 08:05.380
We've been waiting a long time.

08:05.380 --> 08:06.650
Waiting?

08:06.650 --> 08:08.550
You must be the Munya.

08:09.650 --> 08:14.690
Unfortunately, we aren't
this so-called Munya.

08:14.690 --> 08:17.630
I'm sorry, but can we come down there?

08:17.630 --> 08:20.860
I have a lot of things I want to ask you.

08:20.860 --> 08:23.260
The time of our ceremony is approaching

08:23.260 --> 08:25.370
so we cannot greet you well, but...

08:25.370 --> 08:26.530
I don't mind.

08:27.700 --> 08:29.500
Bart, can you hear me?

08:29.500 --> 08:32.440
We're going down to the planet now.

08:32.440 --> 08:33.880
Oh, yeah. Sure...

08:33.880 --> 08:36.280
I'm going to leave things to you.

08:36.280 --> 08:38.350
So take care of the
ship while we're gone.

08:38.350 --> 08:39.710
Are you serious?

08:39.710 --> 08:41.020
Oh, one more thing.

08:41.020 --> 08:43.150
You can't run away from us.

08:43.150 --> 08:45.350
P-Please hold on a minute...

08:45.350 --> 08:46.790
You can't be serious.

09:00.030 --> 09:02.040
I wonder if it's a festival.

09:02.040 --> 09:03.100
Hey!

09:03.100 --> 09:04.900
Hey, let's go over there!

09:06.510 --> 09:07.910
Hey!

09:07.910 --> 09:09.100
Come on!

09:28.600 --> 09:30.030
That shape...

09:34.740 --> 09:36.800
Mr. Alien and Jura...

09:36.800 --> 09:39.640
I wonder what they're doing all alone?

09:41.740 --> 09:43.740
Why don't you calm down a bit?

09:43.740 --> 09:47.110
But he's all alone with Jura!

09:47.110 --> 09:49.080
The captain and vice-captain
are there, too.

09:49.080 --> 09:50.680
But...

09:52.790 --> 09:54.620
Mr. Alien...

10:26.150 --> 10:29.620
- Just like the predictions!
- So the legends were true!

10:29.620 --> 10:30.730
It's the Munya!

10:30.730 --> 10:32.430
The Munya are finally here!

10:32.430 --> 10:33.790
Let's prepare quickly!

10:33.790 --> 10:34.960
Yeah!

10:34.960 --> 10:35.930
Old hag!

10:36.930 --> 10:38.270
Is that you, boy?

10:38.270 --> 10:39.800
It seems you're all right.

10:39.800 --> 10:40.970
What about Jura?

10:40.970 --> 10:43.300
I don't know that crabby chick.

10:43.300 --> 10:44.740
As long as she's fine.

10:44.740 --> 10:46.170
You, come with me.

10:46.170 --> 10:47.160
Sure.

10:52.250 --> 10:54.870
This is the shrine
that leads to the holy path.

10:55.880 --> 10:57.250
So?

10:57.250 --> 11:01.820
What in the world is this Munya
that you're all looking forward to?

11:01.820 --> 11:05.660
They are the ones that guided
our ancestors to this land.

11:05.660 --> 11:07.900
We are grateful to them.

11:07.900 --> 11:10.630
The Munya are the
foundation of Anpathos.

11:11.570 --> 11:13.500
What do they come to do?

11:13.500 --> 11:16.740
The Munya are in need of us.

11:16.740 --> 11:19.510
And we look forward to the Munya.

11:19.510 --> 11:20.910
In need?

11:20.910 --> 11:21.880
Of what?

11:21.880 --> 11:25.110
The Munya are in need of the Spiral Code.

11:25.110 --> 11:27.310
Spiral Code...

11:27.310 --> 11:28.300
What the hell's that?

11:29.650 --> 11:30.910
The spinal cord?

11:33.190 --> 11:35.360
Can we replenish our food and water?

11:35.360 --> 11:38.220
Um, I want to change my locker room...

11:42.500 --> 11:44.290
Please, I've had enough!

11:47.170 --> 11:48.270
What now?

11:48.270 --> 11:49.600
Don't flake out.

11:52.170 --> 11:54.240
Happy times, hard times...

11:54.240 --> 11:59.080
They all have all sorts
of these times ahead of them.

11:59.080 --> 12:02.720
The time that Munya greets
us is the time of our bliss.

12:02.720 --> 12:04.380
Nobody has second thoughts.

12:05.250 --> 12:07.320
You're acting as though nothing is wrong.

12:07.320 --> 12:09.820
But perhaps under your beautiful mask

12:09.820 --> 12:12.590
you're getting goosebumps
from the coming horror?

12:12.590 --> 12:14.460
There is nothing to fear.

12:14.460 --> 12:16.600
Everything is for the Munya.

12:16.600 --> 12:19.260
That is the tradition of Anpathos.

12:25.070 --> 12:26.730
Geez! Quiet!

12:34.050 --> 12:35.220
I-It's the enemy...

12:35.220 --> 12:36.980
- How many?
- Just one.

12:36.980 --> 12:39.750
It's big, like a shipping container.

12:39.750 --> 12:41.360
The harvest ship.

12:41.360 --> 12:43.020
Captain!

12:43.020 --> 12:46.130
It looks like the Munya
you've all been waiting for.

12:46.130 --> 12:47.120
It's here.

12:48.660 --> 12:50.150
The time has finally come.

12:57.770 --> 12:58.740
It's time!

12:58.740 --> 13:00.370
- Let's go to the shrine!
- Yeah!

13:08.320 --> 13:09.520
What is this?

13:09.520 --> 13:11.290
They've put some thought into this.

13:11.290 --> 13:13.490
They're gathered in one spot this way.

13:13.490 --> 13:17.730
I don't want us to be harvested
along with your folklore!

13:17.730 --> 13:20.660
We are not allowed to fight back.

13:20.660 --> 13:21.760
Enough nonsense!

13:21.760 --> 13:23.900
Don't you think this is strange?

13:23.900 --> 13:25.420
That is the tradition.

13:26.970 --> 13:29.330
Old hag, we're going nowhere.

13:30.940 --> 13:32.170
Tradition...

13:32.170 --> 13:33.470
Legend...

13:33.470 --> 13:35.580
Those are convenient words.

13:35.580 --> 13:38.170
For people who can't decide
anything on their own!

13:41.450 --> 13:43.480
Tradition is tradition.

13:43.480 --> 13:45.540
There is no way destiny can change.

13:49.220 --> 13:50.560
What should I do.

13:50.560 --> 13:52.560
There's only one thing.

13:52.560 --> 13:54.900
We'll put up a line of defense here.

13:54.900 --> 13:55.900
Right?

13:55.900 --> 13:57.670
Y-You're right...

13:57.670 --> 13:59.000
Dread team, scramble!

14:00.000 --> 14:00.990
Roger.

14:06.640 --> 14:08.510
Calling all teams.

14:08.510 --> 14:10.850
The objective is to maintain
the defensive line.

14:10.850 --> 14:12.550
Don't chase them too far.

14:12.550 --> 14:13.540
Roger!

14:14.620 --> 14:16.850
This is the correct thing to do.

14:16.850 --> 14:18.390
Are you sure about that?

14:18.390 --> 14:20.220
Why can you say that?

14:20.220 --> 14:22.790
There are no large ships
around here that I can see.

14:22.790 --> 14:27.390
Hanging on to this small piece
of land on this vast marine planet...

14:27.390 --> 14:29.330
What could you know?

14:29.330 --> 14:31.470
What can you realize in your youth?

14:31.470 --> 14:34.100
The most beautiful
planet in the universe?

14:34.100 --> 14:35.870
Have you ever compared?

14:35.870 --> 14:38.540
This has already been decided.

14:38.540 --> 14:41.310
First of all, you barged in here

14:41.310 --> 14:43.280
and then you blaspheme against our god.

14:43.280 --> 14:45.140
There is nothing ruder!

14:47.650 --> 14:49.350
God, huh?

14:49.350 --> 14:52.250
I guess it's useless to talk any further.

14:52.250 --> 14:54.220
I have no choice.

14:54.220 --> 14:55.210
Old hag!

14:55.590 --> 14:57.060
- Ouch...
- Captain?

14:57.060 --> 14:59.260
Of all times for my back to go out.

14:59.260 --> 15:00.760
I can't move like this.

15:00.760 --> 15:02.250
Ouch...

15:04.330 --> 15:08.740
I don't want to be mixed
up in this and die here.

15:08.740 --> 15:09.870
Boy!

15:09.870 --> 15:11.310
Old hag...

15:11.310 --> 15:12.310
Sure!

15:12.310 --> 15:13.300
I gotcha!

15:15.440 --> 15:16.740
Now...

15:16.740 --> 15:19.340
How to waste some time...

15:26.450 --> 15:27.920
Hey, we're launching!

15:28.890 --> 15:31.090
Hey, can't you hear me?

15:31.090 --> 15:32.060
Shut up!

15:32.060 --> 15:33.060
Leave me alone!

15:33.060 --> 15:35.260
How much longer are you gonna sulk?

15:35.260 --> 15:36.600
Look around you!

15:36.600 --> 15:37.460
I don't want to!

15:37.460 --> 15:38.630
Don't you get it?

15:38.630 --> 15:40.860
We're the only ones
who can fight now!

15:42.400 --> 15:43.390
Hey!

15:44.370 --> 15:46.570
It's not my business.

15:46.570 --> 15:47.560
You...

15:52.880 --> 15:55.280
Don't give up on them so easily.

15:55.280 --> 15:57.610
They're your valuable partners, right?

16:04.430 --> 16:08.160
This is when everyone's socks
would've been blown off.

16:08.160 --> 16:10.530
You were gonna save an entire planet.

16:10.530 --> 16:13.190
It's something that
nobody's ever done before.

16:18.570 --> 16:19.900
That's not bad.

16:20.870 --> 16:23.680
In that case, it's time to combine!

16:23.680 --> 16:26.280
I won't forgive you
if you're a slowpoke!

16:26.280 --> 16:28.250
S-Sure...

16:29.450 --> 16:32.080
Women sure change their minds quickly...

16:37.490 --> 16:39.590
They got my control thruster.

16:39.590 --> 16:41.060
I'm heading back for now!

16:41.060 --> 16:44.570
- Enemy approaching the ship!
- Shield down to Level 3!

16:44.570 --> 16:47.470
I won't run. I won't run.
I won't run. I won't run.

16:47.470 --> 16:48.460
Ouch!

16:50.570 --> 16:51.770
We're doomed!

16:51.770 --> 16:53.260
Don't be such a coward!

16:54.640 --> 16:58.370
I've seen countless deaths
around me up until now.

16:59.450 --> 17:02.920
I cursed myself for
my powerlessness each time.

17:02.920 --> 17:06.910
For not being able to do
a single thing for those that died.

17:09.620 --> 17:11.890
How they must have regretted.

17:11.890 --> 17:15.130
Leaving many things undone in their lives.

17:15.130 --> 17:18.590
I feel as if I'm being torn
apart when I remember them.

17:20.470 --> 17:24.510
But even in the very end,
they never gave up then.

17:24.510 --> 17:27.910
They tried to be shining
stars till the very end.

17:27.910 --> 17:31.310
I know wonderful people like that.

17:31.310 --> 17:32.810
Because I know them,

17:32.810 --> 17:37.510
I can't forgive weaklings who
rely on others for their destiny!

17:43.620 --> 17:46.250
- I'll never run!
- Move! You're in the way!

17:49.460 --> 17:51.930
Leave the rest to us and go take a nap...

17:51.930 --> 17:54.160
If you're not quick,
we'll get you with the enemy!

18:12.490 --> 18:16.890
Nobody else can cover
an entire planet like this!

18:16.890 --> 18:18.650
It's too early to celebrate!

18:27.700 --> 18:30.000
I'll give you plenty to eat right now!

18:45.690 --> 18:46.890
That's so reckless.

18:46.890 --> 18:48.650
But I'm a little bit jealous...

18:51.090 --> 18:52.630
Hey, you'll break this thing!

18:52.630 --> 18:53.650
Shut up and watch!

19:01.700 --> 19:03.000
We did it!

19:07.370 --> 19:10.070
I can't honestly be happy about this.

19:18.950 --> 19:21.280
H-How dare you...

19:23.020 --> 19:26.030
Now... you're all free.

19:26.030 --> 19:29.930
From now on, decide for
yourselves when you live and die.

19:31.230 --> 19:35.290
I will never forget your
blasphemy against our god!

19:37.670 --> 19:40.240
A god never says anything.

19:40.240 --> 19:41.610
Doesn't do anything.

19:41.610 --> 19:45.610
And doesn't ask for something in return.

19:45.610 --> 19:48.150
A god just sits and watches over us.

19:48.150 --> 19:51.120
Over foolish humans who are lost.

19:54.920 --> 19:56.580
Sorry to have bothered you.

20:00.790 --> 20:02.200
You didn't videotape it?

20:02.200 --> 20:03.430
What do you mean?

20:03.430 --> 20:05.930
There's no way we
had enough time for that!

20:05.930 --> 20:07.300
Oh well.

20:07.300 --> 20:08.840
In any case, next time

20:08.840 --> 20:12.640
be sure to record the elegance
of my machine on your camera.

20:12.640 --> 20:16.740
I mean, it's so amazing that
it can barrier an entire planet.

20:18.050 --> 20:20.610
Women sure change their minds quickly...

20:22.350 --> 20:24.180
Captain, you must be tired.

20:24.180 --> 20:25.220
You should head to...

20:25.220 --> 20:27.420
No, I have another place to go.

20:27.420 --> 20:28.410
Aye aye.

20:31.890 --> 20:33.060
I'm gonna die...

20:33.060 --> 20:34.720
What's all of this about?

20:36.800 --> 20:40.330
I'm gone for only a little bit
and the entire ship is a wreck!

20:40.330 --> 20:43.040
W-What? What are you talking about?

20:43.040 --> 20:45.870
You don't know just how
hard a time I had, do you?

20:45.870 --> 20:47.570
Right, I don't know.

20:47.570 --> 20:48.780
Oh, I thought so!

20:48.780 --> 20:49.740
Listen.

20:49.740 --> 20:53.910
This happened because you spoil
everyone on a daily basis.

20:53.910 --> 20:55.520
Room assignments, shift changes...

20:55.520 --> 20:58.420
You don't need a report
each and every time, right?

20:58.420 --> 20:59.390
And then

20:59.390 --> 21:02.520
important matters are
decided without consultation!

21:02.520 --> 21:05.590
Even if you are pirates,
there's no excuse!

21:05.590 --> 21:07.060
Well, don't you think so, too?

21:08.230 --> 21:09.200
And?

21:09.200 --> 21:10.330
Wait a minute.

21:10.330 --> 21:11.730
What I mean to say

21:11.730 --> 21:16.300
is that isn't giving me control
of the ship with no warning strange?

21:16.300 --> 21:18.370
Uh, you should've consulted me first.

21:18.370 --> 21:21.410
Well, I'm still
a prisoner strictly speaking...

21:21.410 --> 21:23.840
So consulting me may be strange...

21:32.150 --> 21:37.790
Hey, you realized what the words,

21:37.790 --> 21:43.300
I really wanted to hear are, right?

21:43.300 --> 21:49.540
I was looking at your profile as
you talked about the distant future.

21:49.540 --> 21:59.850
Take me with you to the depths of dreams.

21:59.850 --> 22:02.380
Hey, with all of my body.

22:02.380 --> 22:14.160
A pistol named love shoots
through the center of my chest.

22:14.160 --> 22:25.770
Negotiations and common
sense hold no meaning at all.

22:25.770 --> 22:37.580
Pull the trigger named love and
shoot through my frozen heart.

22:37.580 --> 22:51.450
Pour in your love
to the tips of my fingers.
